plor- ation outside the temple precincts at Mendes suggests the residential area lay to the east and south, with a harbor to the east (Redford 2005: 8). In addition, geophysical surveys have been used at Buto and Tell el-Balamun to reveal much of the Saite settlement (Herbich and Hartung 2004: 16; Herbich and Spencer 2006: 17)." Temple<br>3. TownGovernment administrative building<br>4. Village<br>"Thebes had a special status, at least for a part of the Saite period." <br>'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2089, 'temperature': 0.2})
