d hamlets scatted throughout its rural countryside. State-confederations, located mostly on mountainous regions, are formed by villages and hamlets centered upon an important regional sanctuary. Knossos, Gortyna, and Kydonia were cited by Strabo as the most powerful city-states.  Between 260-240 BCE the power of Knossos seems to have been dominant.  Knossos and Gortyn were the principal political centers of the island until the Roman conquest.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2233, 'temperature': 0.2})
