 the sources that the number of nomadic bu could vary from one thousand tents (i.e. about 4-5 thousand people) to several tens of thousands of people (Taskin 1984, pp. 275-276, 294). Chapter 103 of the Wei shu reports that the Rouran had 10 "nomads\' camps" in 521." <br>"From Chinese chronicles: "They do not have towns surrounded with inner and outer walls, but herd livestock, going from place to place in search of water and grass. Their homes are felt tents, which they take to the place where they stop." " <br>"the Hsiung-nu Huns in China were changing their society ... as attested by the discovery of a city built by them in northwestern China\'s Shaanxi Province in the fifth century C.E."<br>'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2954, 'temperature': 0.2})
